<title>AUSTRIA: EA-Generali 4-mth premium income down.</title>
<headline>EA-Generali 4-mth premium income down.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian insurer EA-Generali said on Tuesday premium income in the first four months of the year eased to 16.39 billion schillings from 16.99 billion in the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>Total claims rose to 8.47 billion schillings from 8.42 billion in the same period of 1995, the Italian-controlled group said in a statement released ahead of a news conference.</p>
<p>Capital investments rose to 128.33 billion schillings compared to 123.32 billion a year earlier, it added.</p>
<p>The group last month reported a 25.1 percent gain in 1996 net profit and said it would pay an unchanged dividend of 17 schillings per share. -- Vienna newsroom, +431 53112 274</p>
